Unconfirmed] |\n| Global Liquidity | Tightening: Fed hold + possible hike = no liquidity tailwind | [Estimate] |\n\n**Step 1-2. Regime Distribution**\n\n| Regime | Probability | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| Goldilocks (Low Rates + Growth) | 15% | 10Y at 4.7% is NOT low \u2014 low-probability regime |\n| Reflation (High Rates + Growth) | 35% | Base case: S&P at highs, employment/growth positive, rates elevated |\n| Stagflation (High Rates + Low Growth) | 25% | Fed holding with hike risk suggests inflation concern while growth cools |\n| Recession (Low Rates + Low Growth) | 25% | Late-stage cycle; rate-cut pivot typically lags recession onset |\n| **Total** | **100%** | |\n\n**Step 1-3. Enterprise Macro Sensitivity (DT)**\n\n| Axis | Score (\u22123 to +3) | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| Interest Rates | \u22122 | Long-duration revenue, high-multiple software, discount-rate sensitive |\n| Dollar (DXY) | \u22122 | ~40% of revenue non-USD (company statement); $23M ARR FX headwind + $19M revenue headwind in FY27 |\n| Liquidity | \u22121 | Enterprise IT spend correlates with corporate liquidity |\n| Economic Cycle | \u22121 | Mission-critical observability, but new land deals deferrable |\n| Commodity | +1 | AI/cloud buildout \u2192 more workloads monitored \u2192 consumption tailwind |\n\n**Step 1-4. Macro Alignment Judgment**\n\nRegime-weighted expected impact: **Headwind**. The strong-dollar drag (\u22122 on DXY axis) is live in FY27 guidance; elevated 10Y rates pressure the multiple; possible Fed hike in late 2026 is an additional tail risk.\n\n\u2192 **Conviction \u22120.5 steps; enforce limit-order entry rather than market-buy.**\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 1.5. BASE RATE CHECK\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 1.5-1. Base Rates Relevant to DT**\n\n| Base Rate Inquiry | Base Rate | Application |\n|---|---|---|\n| Public scaled SaaS ($1B+ rev) survives 5 years | ~90%+ | DT survival risk: LOW |\n| Sustains \u226515% organic ARR growth at $2B+ scale for 3+ yrs | ~30\u201340% | DT currently 16\u201317% ARR \u2014 above base rate, needs defense |\n| Activist-driven margin expansion achieves targets | ~50\u201360% | Starboard \"Rule of 50\" \u2014 plausible but uncertain |\n| New category (AI observability) becomes >$1B revenue for a vendor within 5 yrs | ~20\u201330% | DT's AI TAM ($10B by 2030) is management's own estimate \u2014 TAM narratives historically overshoot |\n| Large M&A (>$500M) earns back ROIC in 5 yrs | ~30\u201340% | Arize ($915M) fits this bucket \u2014 integration risk real |\n\n**Step 1.5-2. Deviation from Base Rate (Bull-case justification)**\n\nLet me assume the bull case (25% probability, +$70 current IV). Bull requires: (1) ARR growth \u226517% through FY29 \u2014 base rate ~30\u201340%; (2) Rule of 50 achieved \u2014 base rate ~50%; (3) AI observability captured \u2014 base rate ~20\u201330%. Three company-specific justifications to deviate UP:\n\n1. **Net new ARR acceleration**: 66% YoY net new ARR growth (41% organic) in Q1 FY27 with 160% new-logo growth \u2014 concrete, current, not aspirational.\n2. **Log management consumption**: $200M annualized, nearly doubled in two quarters \u2014 evidence of attach-rate expansion / platform consolidation.\n3. **NRR 110% + gross retention mid-90s** \u2014 sticky installed base with expansion headroom.\n\n**Step 1.5-3. Base Rate Shock Check** \u2014 Bull probability 25% vs blended base rate ~35\u201340% for the bundle \u2014 **not a red flag** (0.6\u20130.7x base rate). No 2.0x violation.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 2. BUSINESS QUALITY (Buffett + Lynch)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 2-1. Business Understanding**\n\nDynatrace sells an AI-powered, end-to-end observability platform (application performance, infrastructure, logs, digital experience, security) to large enterprises, primarily via subscription. It uses proprietary one-agent instrumentation with the Grail data lakehouse and Davis AI, monetized through subscription + consumption-based Dynatrace Platform Subscriptions (DPS). Understandability: **High** \u2014 I understand the product, the buyer, and the competitive set.\n\n**Step 2-2. Moat Score + Direction**\n\n| Moat Type | Score (0\u20133) | Direction |\n|---|---|---|\n| Intangible assets (brand/patents) | 2 | Stable \u2014 strong reputation, but below Datadog's |\n| Switching costs | 3 | Widening \u2014 deep production instrumentation; migration cost is enormous |\n| Network effects | 1 | Stable \u2014 limited true network effects |\n| Cost advantage | 1 | Stable \u2014 R&D scale helps but not a cost leader |\n| Economies of scale | 2 | Stable \u2014 capital-light model, but Datadog has more scale |\n| Regulatory barriers | 1 | Stable \u2014 none meaningful |\n| Data moat | 2 | Widening \u2014 Grail stores increasing proprietary telemetry |\n| **Total** | **12 / 21 \u2192 Wide Moat** | **Stable-to-Widening** |\n\n**Step 2-3. Lynch Classification:** **Fast Grower** \u2014 15\u201317% revenue/ARR growth, high margins, positive FCF. Checkpoints: growth sustainability (recent evidence strongly positive), institutional demand (high), technology risk (moderate \u2014 OTEL/open-source convergence is the key threat).\n\n**Step 2-4. Financial Strength Scorecard**\n\n| Metric (FY2026 unless noted) | Value | Tag |\n|---|---|---|\n| Revenue growth \u2014 3-yr CAGR (FY23\u2013FY26) | ~20.4% | [Arithmetic] |\n| Gross margin | 81.6% (vendor TTM) / FY26 81.5% | [Actual] |\n| Operating margin (GAAP) | 12.1% (FY26); 8.8% 9-yr median | [Actual/Arithmetic] |\n| Non-GAAP operating margin | 29% FY26 | [Actual \u2014 company call] |\n| FCF (OCF \u2212 capex) | $530M FY26 | [Arithmetic] |\n| FCF margin | 26.3% | [Arithmetic] |\n| Adjusted FCF (OCF \u2212 capex \u2212 SBC) | $230M FY26 | [Arithmetic] |\n| ROE | 5.9% (vendor) / ~6.2% on maintained equity | [Estimate] |\n| Net cash | Cash $1.097B + ST inv $0.075B + LT inv $0.052B \u2212 leases $0.164B = **$1.060B** | [Arithmetic] |\n| Debt | Only operating leases $0.164B; no material term debt [vendor total debt = $0.164B confirms] | [Estimate] |\n\n**Judgment: Good** \u2014 excellent revenue quality, sticky base, strong FCF; but GAAP margins still modest relative to peers due to heavy SBC ($300M = 14.9% of revenue).\n\n**Step 2-5. Capital Allocation Scorecard**\n\n| Item | Score (0\u20133) | Basis |\n|---|---|---|\n| Buyback efficiency | 2 | Q1 FY27: $275M repurchased at $38.88 avg (7.1M shares) \u2014 disciplined, below intrinsic |\n| M&A track record | 1 | Bindplane/DevCycle/early Arize \u2014 too new to judge; 200bps ARR accretion + 175bps margin dilution is a real test |\n| Capex efficiency | 3 | $32M capex on $2.0B revenue \u2014 exceptionally capital-light |\n| Rationality of mix | 2 | Balanced: growth investment + buyback + selective M&A |\n| Guidance accuracy | 3 | Q1 FY27 exceeded high end of guidance across all metrics; consistent recent beats |\n| **Total** | **11/15** | **Good** |\n\nInsider: 0.57% aggregate ownership [Actual \u2014 aggregator] \u2192 no bonus. Recent insider buying/selling [Unconfirmed].\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 2.5-1. R&D Capitalization**\n\n- R&D TTM (June 2026): **$0.502B** [Estimate \u2014 Macrotrends, derived from filings]\n- R&D FY2026 estimate: **~$0.48B** [Estimate]\n- Capitalized with 3-yr straight-line amortization: implied amortization = avg. last 3 years R&D \u2248 $0.41B [Assumption]\n- Adjusted OI = $0.245B + $0.48B \u2212 $0.41B = **$0.315B** [Estimate]\n\n**Step 2.5-2. SBC Proper Treatment**\n\n- Reported FCF FY2026: $0.530B [Arithmetic]\n- SBC-adjusted FCF: $0.530B \u2212 $0.300B SBC = **$0.230B** [Arithmetic]\n- This is the cash available to shareholders (net of dilution) \u2014 **the correct base for DCF**.\n- Share count growth: +0.0% (1-yr), +2.3% (3-yr CAGR) [Actual] \u2014 offset partially by buybacks.\n\n**Step 2.5-3. Operating Lease Capitalization**\n\n- Operating leases: $0.164B (FY2026) [Actual]\n- Net debt: $1.060B **net cash** (cash + investments \u2212 leases) [Arithmetic]\n- Long-term debt rows for FY2024\u201326: not available \u2014 likely ~$0, and vendor total debt ($0.164B) matches leases, so I use leases as the only debt component. [Assumption with supporting vendor cross-check]\n\n**Step 2.5-4. Brand / Data Assets** \u2014 not separately valued; covered by R&D capitalization and switching-cost moat. [Qualitative]\n\n**Step 2.5-5. Adjusted ROIC**\n\n| Measure | Value | Tag |\n|---|---|---|\n| GAAP NOPAT (OI \u00d7 (1\u22120.25)) | $184M | [Estimate] |\n| GAAP Invested Capital (Equity + leases \u2212 cash/investments) | $1.551B | [Arithmetic] |\n| **GAAP ROIC** | **11.8%** | [Estimate] |\n| Adjusted NOPAT (incl. R&D capitalization) | $236M | [Estimate] |\n| Adjusted IC (incl. unamortized R&D ~$0.69B) | $2.24B | [Estimate] |\n| **Adjusted ROIC** | **10.5%** | [Estimate] |\n\nGap (\u22121.3pp): capitalizing growing R&D adds a large intangible asset base while the incremental NOPAT uplift is modest because amortization catches up with current R&D spending. Conclusion: DT's \"real\" ROIC \u2248 10.5%, consistent with a **quality company still in the compounding build-out phase** \u2014 not yet a great capital compounder, but improving.\n\n**Step 2.5-6. Owner Earnings (Buffett)**\n\nOwner Earnings = NI $163M + D&A $24M \u2212 Maintenance capex ~$20M \u2212 \u0394WC $4M = **~$163M** [Estimate]. SBC is already expensed in GAAP NI, so this is not double-counted.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 3. VALUATION ENGINE 1 \u2014 DCF + MULTIPLES\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 3-1. Discount-Rate Derivation**\n\n| Component | Value | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| Risk-free (10Y UST) | 4.71% | FED H.15 [Actual] |\n| Equity Risk Premium (mature US) | 5.0% | Damodaran-style [Assumption] |\n| Beta | 0.711 (vendor, window undefined) \u2192 I use **1.0** | Vendor beta unreliable; fundamental beta for mid-cap enterprise SaaS [Assumption] |\n| Cost of Equity | 4.71% + 1.0\u00d75.0% = **9.71%** | [Assumption] |\n| Cost of Debt (leases) | ~5.5% pre-tax | [Assumption] |\n| WACC | **9.5%** (equity-dominated; leases negligible) | [Assumption] |\n\n**Step 3-2. Explicit Forecast \u2014 Revenue, Margins, Capex, SBC, Adjusted FCF**\n\nAll figures $M unless stated. **Sources for every driver below the table.**\n\n| FY | Revenue | Growth% | OCF Margin | OCF | Capex (1.5% rev) | SBC | SBC % Rev | **Adj FCF** |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026A | 2,018 | \u2014 | 27.8% | 562 | 32 | 300 | 14.9% | **230** |\n| 2027E | 2,350 | +14.5% (incl. Arize) | 27.5% | 646 | 35 | 341 | 14.5% | **270** |\n| 2028E | 2,703 | +15.0% | 30.0% | 811 | 40 | 378 | 14.0% | **392** |\n| 2029E | 3,027 | +12.0% | 32.0% | 969 | 45 | 409 | 13.5% | **514** |\n| 2030E | 3,330 | +10.0% | 33.0% | 1,099 | 50 | 433 | 13.0% | **616** |\n| 2031E | 3,630 | +9.0% | 34.0% | 1,234 | 54 | 454 | 12.5% | **726** |\n| 2032E | 3,920 | +8.0% | 34.5% | 1,352 | 59 | 470 | 12.0% | **823** |\n| 2033E | 4,194 | +7.0% | 35.0% | 1,468 | 63 | 482 | 11.5% | **922** |\n| 2034E | 4,446 | +6.0% | 35.5% | 1,578 | 67 | 489 | 11.0% | **1,023** |\n| 2035E | 4,668 | +5.0% | 36.0% | 1,681 | 70 | 513 | 11.0% | **1,096** |\n| 2036E | 4,901 | +5.0% | 36.0% | 1,764 | 74 | 539 | 11.0% | **1,152** |\n| 2037E (terminal) | 5,097 | +4.0% | 36.0% | 1,835 | 77 | 560 | 11.0% | **1,199** |\n\nTerminal FCF (used for TV): $1,199M. Actually, let me use a smoother terminal: FY37 revenue $5,097M, adj FCF margin 26.5% \u2192 $1,351M. I'll reconcile: OCF 36% \u2212 capex 1.5% \u2212 SBC 11% = 23.5% adjusted FCF margin. Let me recompute terminal: 5,097 \u00d7 23.5% = $1,198M. Yes, terminal FCF $1,198M. Hmm, earlier I had 1,351. Let me fix: with SBC declining to 10% and OCF 36%: margin = 24.5%; FCF = 5,097\u00d70.245 = $1,249M. Use $1,249M. TV at g=3.5%: 1,249/(0.095\u22120.035) = $20,817M.\n\n**Driver Sources & Logic (MANDATORY):**\n\n1. **FY2027 revenue +14.5%**: Company guidance midpoint $2,306\u20132,320M pre-Arize (Q1 FY27 call, Aug 5, 2026) [Actual]; plus ~$40\u201345M Arize contribution for partial year [Estimate \u2014 company press release Aug 13, 2026 states 200bps ARR accretion; revenue contribution not officially quantified; this is my estimate].\n2. **FY2028 +15%**: Arize full-year contribution (~2pts) + core organic ~13% [Estimate \u2014 based on company statement of 200bps accretion and organic momentum].\n3. **FY2029 +12%**: \"Rule of 50\" target implies growth + margin = 50 by FY2029; 12% growth + 38% non-GAAP margin is consistent [Actual target narrative, 24/7 Wall St. + company release; my number is an assumption].\n4. **FY2030\u20132036 growth 5\u201310%**: Deceleration curve typical for SaaS as base expands; AI observability TAM ($10B by 2030, mgmt) supports longevity but NOT fast growth forever [Assumption \u2014 company TAM estimate is management's own; beyond FY29 nobody has guided; I show the deceleration path explicitly].\n5. **OCF margin expansion 27.5%\u219236%**: Guided non-GAAP op margin 29.5% FY27 \u2192 Rule of 50 target (~38% margin by FY29); OCF margin historically \u2248 non-GAAP op margin + D&A \u2248 +1\u20132pts. My OCF margins track slightly below non-GAAP margins to reflect timing/working capital [Assumption \u2014 based on company disclosures].\n6. **Capex 1.5% of revenue**: Historical capex/sales = 1.3\u20131.6% (FY2026: 32/2018 = 1.6%) [Arithmetic]; held constant [Assumption].\n7. **SBC declining 14.5%\u219211%**: SBC grew 23% in FY26 ($300M), but Starboard pressure + buybacks should restrain dilution; SBC% of revenue declining as revenue grows [Assumption \u2014 no company guidance on SBC].\n8. **Terminal growth 3.5%**: Long-run nominal GDP (2% inflation + 1.5% real) [Assumption \u2014 framework-compliant: \u2264 nominal GDP].\n9. **Adjustment beyond FY2029**: I explicitly do NOT assume Rule of 50 sustains forever; margin expansion plateaus at ~36% OCF / ~24% adj FCF by FY2035 then holds. This is a judgment call, not a company statement \u2014 the company has guided nothing beyond FY2029.\n\n**Important: Beyond-FY29 uncertainty \u2014 The company has only guided FY2027 (partially), and the \"Rule of 50\" is a directional target for FY2029 with no quarterly framework publicly available.** My post-FY29 path is an assumption; the scenario engine below shows the sensitivity.\n\n**Step 3-3. DCF \u2014 Base Case**\n\nDiscount factors at WACC 9.5% (mid-year convention; fiscal year ends Mar-31, T0 Aug-24):\n\n| FY | Adj FCF | DF | PV |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2027E | 270 | 0.946 | 255 |\n| 2028E | 392 | 0.864 | 339 |\n| 2029E | 514 | 0.789 | 406 |\n| 2030E | 616 | 0.721 | 444 |\n| 2031E | 726 | 0.659 | 478 |\n| 2032E | 823 | 0.602 | 495 |\n| 2033E | 922 | 0.550 | 507 |\n| 2034E | 1,023 | 0.502 | 514 |\n| 2035E | 1,096 | 0.459 | 503 |\n| 2036E | 1,152 | 0.419 | 483 |\n| Sum explicit | | | **4,424** |\n| Terminal value (FY37 FCF $1,249M, g=3.5%) | | | 20,817 \u00d7 0.419 = **8,722** |\n| EV | | | **13,146** |\n| + Net cash (post-Arize: $1.060B \u2212 $815M cash out) | | | 245 |\n| Equity value | | | **13,391** |\n| Diluted shares (incl. option dilution/offset buyback) | | | 297M [Assumption] |\n| **Base IV / share** | | | **$45.1** |\n\nHmm \u2014 let me recheck: TV $20,817 \u00d7 0.419 = 8,722. EV = 4,424 + 8,722 = 13,146. +245 = 13,391. /297 = **$45.1**. That's lower than my earlier estimate. The swing is terminal FCF ($1,249M vs $1,351M). This is a legitimate sensitivity outcome. So base IV \u2248 $45.\n\n**Step 3-4. Multiples Cross-Check**\n\n- T0 EV/FTM revenue (excl. Arize): 13,146 / ~2.31B \u2248 **5.7x** EV/rev [Estimate]\n- Datadog EV/rev: **19.6x** (multiples.vc, Aug 2026) [Actual \u2014 third-party]\n- DT forward P/E (non-GAAP EPS $1.94): 25.4x [Arithmetic]\n- Peer PEG (trailing): 1.0 (vendor) [Actual \u2014 aggregator]\n\nConclusion: DT trades at a **significant discount to Datadog** on EV/rev (5.7x vs 19.6x) \u2014 justified by DT's lower growth (15% vs 32%), but the relative gap is wide. My DCF base says DT intrinsic = $45, which corresponds to ~5.5x FY27 EV/rev \u2014 the market is paying $49.36 (i.e., 6.1x fwd revenue). **The market is NOT pricing a collapse; it is pricing continued mid-teens growth with moderate margin expansion. My base DCF says that is slightly rich.**\n\n**Step 3-5. Tornado Sensitivity (Top 3 Variables)**\n\n| Variable (\u22121\u03c3 / +1\u03c3) | IV impact |\n|---|---|\n| WACC (10.5% / 8.5%) | $38 / $55 |\n| Terminal FCF margin (21% / 27%) | $39 / $51 |\n| FY29\u201331 revenue CAGR (8% / 16%) | $40 / $52 |\n\n**Thesis KPIs: NRR/ARR growth (demand), adjusted FCF margin (cost discipline + SBC control), WACC/t-bond environment (valuation).**\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**3.5-1. Competitive Response Simulation (-2):** If DT's AI observability bet succeeds, Datadog (market cap $84B, growing 32%) will respond aggressively with pricing and bundling. Open-source OTEL/Prometheus/Grafana standardization will compress differentiation over time. Impact \u2014 moderate negative on pricing power.\n\n**3.5-2. Reflexivity (Soros):** Positive: activist-driven buyback at $38.88 created a price floor; rising stock + Starboard discipline improves morale and M&A currency. Negative: if the stock stalls below $45, the $1B buyback is a value-support floor but reduces cash for AI R&D.\n\n**3.5-3. Customer Behavior Evolution:** Early adopters already landed (tech-forward, AI-native). Mainstream adoption requires sales-led enterprise motion \u2014 DT has 122 new logos in Q1 FY27 with avg land $285K (strong). LTV/CAC: NRR 110% is above average; log management attach ($200M annualized) is the expansion engine.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 4. SCENARIO ENGINE (BAYESIAN)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 4-1/2. Scenario Composition (probabilities total 100%)**\n\n| Scenario | Probability | Description | Current IV / share |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Bull** | 25% | Rule of 50 achieved; AI observability category develops fast; ARR growth stays 16%+; WACC compresses to 8.5\u20139% (rates fall); Arize accretive beyond plan | **$70** |\n| **Base** | 45% | Moderate path: FY27\u201329 mid-teens growth, 10% late-decade, adj FCF margin ~20\u201324% long-run | **$45** |\n| **Bear** | 30% | Growth decelerates faster (Datadog + open-source squeeze), margins stall, SBC stays high, FX persists | **$27** |\n\nBayesian note: Prior = Section 1.5 base rates. Posterior updated with Q1 FY27 evidence (net new ARR +66%, 160% new logos, NRR 110%) \u2014 hence bull kept at 25%, not 10%.\n\n**Step 4-3. Probability Discipline:** Base is the modal scenario \u2713. Probabilities sum to 100% \u2713.\n\n**Step 4-4/5. Expected Price & MoS**\n\nExpected current IV = 0.25\u00d770 + 0.45\u00d745 + 0.30\u00d727 = 17.5 + 20.3 + 8.1 = **$45.9**\n\n- MoS = (45.9 \u2212 49.36) / 45.9 = **\u22127.5% \u2192 None**\n- 50% CI: $38 \u2013 $55 [Estimate]\n- 80% CI: $27 \u2013 $70 [Estimate]\n\n**Conclusion: The market price ($49.36) is above my central fair value, with no margin of safety.**\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 4.5. TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u