2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n**Archetype: B \u2014 Quality Compounder (Engine 1: DCF + Multiples)**\n\nReasons for archetype selection:\n1. Subscription revenue is ~95% of total revenue; gross margin 81.6% [Actual FY26 TTM]; this is a recurring-revenue software business, not a hardware hybrid.\n2. Revenue CAGR 23.5% over 5 fiscal years [Actual], with NRR 110% and mid-90s gross retention [Estimate \u2014 company-prepared remarks, Q1 FY27 call].\n3. Expanding profitability: GAAP operating margin 8.0% (FY23) \u2192 12.1% (FY26); non-GAAP op. margin 30% (FY26) [Actual].\n4. FCF positive and net-cash balance sheet; FCF margin 26% (FY26) [Actual].\n5. The customer base and switching costs are high: platform embedded in production environments, 16 consecutive Gartner MQ Leadership [Actual \u2014 company press release].\n\nEngine selection rationale:\n- Engine 4 (expectation-driven) would over-value the AI-observability optionality and is not required \u2014 the current business already carries the value.\n- Engine 3 (hybrid) is inappropriate: no meaningful hardware installed base.\n- Engine 1 with an explicit owner-earnings definition is appropriate, because the company is a quality compounder but GAAP earnings are suppressed by SBC, so a cash-flow definition must be built deliberately (Section 2.5).\n\nTransition status: **None**. The company is not transitioning between archetypes; the DPS pricing shift is a monetization model evolution within the same archetype.\n\nI declare the data pack adequate for this analysis, with four critical gaps I must carry:\n- **[Unconfirmed]** \u2014 R&D is not in the pack; I sourced a third-party estimate (TTM Jun-2026 R&D $0.502B, Macrotrends [Estimate]).\n- **[Unconfirmed]** \u2014 Arize acquisition ($915M, announced Aug-2026) terms/funding not established.\n- **[Unconfirmed]** \u2014 Net debt components: our long-term debt column only; I have reconstructed a balance-sheet net cash figure with named components.\n- **[Unconfirmed]** \u2014 FY27 GAAP OCF is not directly guided; I have estimated it from adjusted FCF guidance.\n\n\nSECTION 1. MACRO CONTEXT\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n**Step 1-1. Macro Variable Check (as of T0, Aug-2026)**\n\n| Variable | Level / Direction | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| 10-yr Treasury | 4.74% (Aug 21), elevated, upward drift | [Actual] \u2014 Fed H.15, 2026-08-24 |\n| 2-yr Treasury | 4.24% | [Actual] \u2014 Fed H.15 |\n| 5-yr TIPS real yield | 2.09% | [Actual] \u2014 Fed H.15 |\n| 10-yr TIPS real yield | 2.40% | [Actual] \u2014 Fed H.15 |\n| Fed funds effective | 3.63% | [Actual] \u2014 Fed H.15 |\n| DXY | Directionally firm in 2026 (DT guidance cites $19M FY27 revenue FX headwind and $23M ARR headwind) | [Estimate] \u2014 company guidance implies dollar strength |\n| Inflation breakeven (10y) | ~2.3% | [Arithmetic] \u2014 nominal minus TIPS |\n| Credit spreads | Not sourced; no material DT credit risk | [Unconfirmed] \u2014 not a governing input |\n| Fed stance | Policy rate 3.63% vs ~2.3% breakeven \u2192 real policy rate ~1.3%, mildly restrictive; market is pricing normalization/cuts | [Estimate] \u2014 inferred from H.15; FOMC statement not retrieved |\n\n**Step 1-2. Regime Classification**\n\n| Regime | Probability | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| Goldilocks | 35% | Enterprise software demand remains solid (DT record new-logo growth +160% YoY, Q1 FY27 [Actual]); 10-yr high at 4.7% but policy rate is already 3.63% |\n| Reflation | 40% | Growth is still above trend and rates are elevated; value/cyclicals favored, but DT can still compound |\n| Stagflation | 15%